<VI _name="lvai_wire_dyn_events.vi" description="Wire a VI's event registration refnum onto its Event Structure's DYNAMIC EVENT terminal - the one connection AIXML cannot express, and therefore the only thing a regeneration loses.\0A\0ATWO SOURCES, TRIED IN THAT ORDER. Preferred\3A the structure's own Event Registration Refnum TUNNEL, whose net is BRANCHED - authoring that tunnel in AIXML is what makes the whole route survive a regeneration, so it is the shape to write. Fallback\3A the Register For Events node on the block diagram, wired straight across the loop border, which LabVIEW accepts and answers by creating the tunnel itself - measured. The fallback assumes ONE such node in the VI and reports how many it saw.\0A\0AHOW BOTH ENDS ARE IDENTIFIED - BY NAME, never by index. The structure's terminals answer to the literal Event Registration Refnum, the node's to the lower-case event registration refnum, because a terminal's name comes from its data type or its node's label rather than from a user label. The node's refnum output is picked as 'a source that is not named error out', which needs no spelling of the refnum at all.\0A\0AAuto Route? (F) IS WIRED TRUE, AND THAT IS NOT OPTIONAL. With its FALSE default the connection is registered in every readable form - signal termList, the terminal's bit 15, a grown compressedWireTable, a live Connected Wire, Is Broken? false, the VI unbroken - and LabVIEW's renderer draws NOTHING. Position and Bounds are identical between the two cases, so no property can tell them apart and CleanUpWire changes neither.\0A\0AWHAT IT REPORTS AS THE EFFECT is the DESTINATION terminal's own wire\3A none before, one that is not broken after. That is route-independent, where an end COUNT is not - branching the tunnel's net gives a wire of three ends and crossing the loop border gives a fresh one of two.\0A\0ATHE SEARCH IS TWO LEVELS DEEP\3A the block diagram, and the diagrams of every WhileLoop, ForLoop, TimedLoop and CaseStructure on it - which covers a front-panel event loop as NI's own templates build one. Class Name carries NO SPACES (WhileLoop, EventStructure). A deeper structure is not found, and the class names seen at the top level are reported so that reads as a miss rather than a mystery.\0A\0AONE PROPERTY NODE PER REFERENCE, and no Connected Wire on a terminal not established as wired\3A that read is what invalidated the references following it in a probe, and it is why the tunnel branch here runs on an error path of its own.">
